FINAL SELF-AUDIT CHECKLIST
Complete this checklist only at Gate 5:
•	Every learning objective is addressed in the text.
•	Every relevant NMC competency is correctly quoted from the supplied source.
•	No NMC competency code, domain, or level has been invented or inferred.
•	Competencies not covered are explicitly stated.
•	Every important numerical claim has a traceable source.
•	Every dose, route, frequency, maximum dose and half-life has a traceable source.
•	Renal, hepatic, pediatric and other relevant adjustments are addressed.
•	No citation, PMID, DOI, NCT number, guideline year or numerical value has been fabricated.
•	Current guideline versions are the most recent that could be verified.
•	Guideline recommendation systems are reported using their native terminology.
•	Evidence certainty is not confused with recommendation strength.
•	Regulatory approval status is stated with jurisdiction and year where applicable.
•	Indian regulatory status is not inferred from FDA/EMA approval.
•	Off-label uses are explicitly identified.
•	Efficacy evidence is distinguished from regulatory approval.
•	Evidence quality is distinguished from applicability.
•	Conflicting guidelines are explicitly presented rather than silently harmonized.
•	Conflicting doses are explicitly presented with jurisdiction and indication.
•	Important negative evidence is included where clinically relevant.
•	Investigational agents are clearly distinguished from approved therapies.
•	Every figure has an original brief and caption.
•	No copied or closely adapted artwork is included.
•	Every table answers a defined teaching question.
•	Tables are independently constructed and appropriately sourced.
•	Abbreviations are defined at first use.
•	Generic/INN names are used appropriately.
•	Units are appropriate and SI-compliant.
•	Word count is within the permitted range.
•	Section word budgets are reasonably balanced.
•	Contradictions with preceding/following chapters are flagged.
•	Genuine uncertainties and limitations are explicitly stated.
•	Quotation log is complete.
•	Potential copyright-permission requirements are flagged.
•	Claims audit is complete.
•	Reference verification audit is complete.
•	AI disclosure is included.
•	Conflict-of-interest placeholder is included.
•	Final .docx contains no unapproved new scientific content.
